# .editorconfig has said `end_of_line = lf` since the first commit, but nothing
# enforced it: with no attributes file, core.autocrlf converts on checkout and
# the working tree on Windows is CRLF against an LF-declared convention.
#
# That is not cosmetic. test/workers/setup.ts strips SQL comments with /--.*$/,
# and in JavaScript `.` does not match \r while `$` does not match before one —
# so on a CRLF checkout every comment in schema.sql survives the strip, the
# whole file collapses into one commented-out line, and the D1 tests fail with
# "SQL code did not contain a statement". On Linux CI the same code is green,
# which is the worst shape a bug can have.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and the first two never reach git anyway.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
